"notes": "Modified cash basis school district; all funds governmental (Nutrition is a governmental fund here), so business_type is null. Beginning cash = total governmental fund balance at start of year (14,813,289, p4), ending cash 13,831,219 (balance sheet p5, also p2). Pages: p1 Statement of Activities, p2 net position, p3-5 governmental fund statements, p6-7 General Fund components, p8-11 General Fund budget schedule, p12-18 other fund budget schedules. Transfers 165,000 GF to Nutrition (net zero in total). Hidden transfer: General Fund components (p7) reclassifies 300,000 out of Operation and maintenance of plant as the GF transfer to the Depreciation Fund; the GF budget schedule's O&M lines (1,524,033) include it, so detail has a contra line -300,000 plus other financing -300,000 (GF) and +300,000 (Depreciation Fund receipt); the basic statements already show 1,224,033. State categorical (15,838) and federal programs (473,009) lines are recorded under instruction because the statement (p3) reclassifies them to Instruction (8,031,220 + 488,847 = 8,520,067). Debt service not split between principal and interest anywhere, recorded as principal with review. Non-revenue receipts 45,961 split into sale 2,000 and other 43,961 using fund schedules. No per-account student activities schedule; Activities Fund one-line budget schedule used. Exhibit of cash disbursements by object (Exhibit N) not in the trimmed pages, so General Fund expenditures are 'not itemized'. Special Building 5400 loan proceeds shown only as budget (3,085,210), actual nil, not recorded. Fund balances: Nutrition beginning (3,975) per p15 versus restated mapping on p4; totals tie. Read pages 1-18 of 18"
